    "writing": {
      "id": "writing",
      "name": "Writing",
      "group": "Academic",
      "stat": "Mind",
      "cost": "1 Point / Level (Constituent) / Multi-Genre by table",
      "specialisations": "Academic, Fiction, Journalistic, Poetic, Religious, Technical",
      "source": "BESM Extras (Chapter 2: Skills)",
      "fullDescription": "Multi-Genre Cost: 1 Point/Level\nRelevant Stat: Average of Mind and Soul\nSpecialisations: Academic, Fiction, Journalistic, Poetic,\nReligious, Technical The ability to communicate ideas or emotions in a written work, though a person without this Skill may still know how to read and write. 02:\n\nVARYING SKILL COSTS VARYING SKILL COSTS BY GENRE BY GENRE The Point cost of a Skill is based on its utility in the game and not on the difficulty of learning the Skill. Otherwise, highly detailed and technical (such as sciences and medical/engineering fields) would always be the most costly, regardless of their utility within the game. Table-03: Genre Skill Costs provides a list of Character Point costs for 30 popular gaming genres, settings, and themes, as well as a default multi-genre cost that represents an average for use in games where the genre or setting frequently changes. For example, in a typical action-adventure setting, the action, scientific, and tech are fairly costly; conversely, the humanistic, diplomatic, and business are inexpensive. The reverse is true in a “slice of life” setting. Similarly, investigation and sleuthing are costly in a detective setting, but inexpensive for adventures during the Age of Discovery. Use Table-03 as a guideline for determining how much a particular hould be worth in your particular campaign. The 30 game genres provided aren’t strictly defined and offer flexibility in interpretation, though their names likely evoke a strong understanding of their scopes for player groups. Of course, not every possible genre could be listed, and so consideration is necessary. MODERN DAY CAMPAIGNS Action Adventure, Animal Adventures, Classic Horror, Detective, Loony Cartoons, Romantic Comedy, Slice of Life, Spy Thriller, and Supernatural Occult FANTAS"
    },
