      "name": "Physical Sciences (Physics)",
      "group": "Scientific",
      "stat": "Mind",
      "cost": "1 Point / Level (Constituent) / Multi-Genre by table",
      "specialisations": "Acoustics, Electromagnetism, Nuclear, Optics, Particle Physics, Quantum Mechanics, Thermodynamics",
      "source": "BESM Extras (Chapter 2: Skills)",
      "fullDescription": "Multi-Genre Cost: 2 Points/Level\nRelevant Stat: Mind\nSpecialisations: Alchemy, Astronomy, Biochemistry,\nChemistry, Mathematics, Physics Scientific training in the way the physical realm functions and manifests itself as reality, including the necessary background knowledge concerning universal laws and constants. 02:\n\nMany Race and Class Templates provided in the BESM RPG and its expansions use the Skill Group Attribute instead of individual . To translate these Templates for use with , reassign the total Character Points allocated in the combined Skill Group to the new Attribute (page 8). Then, use the Skill Points provided to acquire one or more individual that cover a similar range of knowledge and talent as the Template’s original Skill Groups. This reassignment method maintains the same total Template Point cost, while simultaneously ensuring game balance. TEMPLATES AND"
